1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,800
(Episode 6)

2
00:00:10,017 --> 00:00:14,873
The heads of the Koutokukai and
the Kirii-gumi are mortal enemies.

3
00:00:14,898 --> 00:00:17,476
You said a war might break out
the moment they cross paths...

4
00:00:18,877 --> 00:00:20,277
We're in deep trouble.

5
00:00:56,974 --> 00:00:58,600
Some things never change.

6
00:01:03,897 --> 00:01:06,697
Kei-chan, I missed you so much!

7
00:01:08,817 --> 00:01:10,117
Let's get married!

8
00:01:10,797 --> 00:01:12,434
Kei-chan!

9
00:01:12,517 --> 00:01:13,817
Whoa.

10
00:01:17,337 --> 00:01:18,637
I'll kill you.

11
00:01:19,557 --> 00:01:20,664
Kei-chan?

12
00:01:21,937 --> 00:01:23,234
I'm gonna kill you!

13
00:01:23,317 --> 00:01:24,617
Huh?

14
00:01:25,137 --> 00:01:26,437
This means all-out war!

15
00:01:28,417 --> 00:01:29,965
Come on, what war, Kei-chan?!

16
00:01:30,957 --> 00:01:32,257
Get off me!

17
00:01:33,218 --> 00:01:34,357
Wait up!

18
00:01:35,517 --> 00:01:37,617
Or how about a tank? Do you want a tank?

19
00:01:38,377 --> 00:01:40,034
You want a tank more than a whole city?

20
00:01:40,117 --> 00:01:41,614
Or do you want me?

21
00:01:41,697 --> 00:01:43,397
You're the last thing I need!

22
00:02:49,400 --> 00:02:51,385
"The Journey To Killing You Season 2"

23
00:03:17,322 --> 00:03:18,356
What's wrong?

24
00:03:43,056 --> 00:03:44,391
I thought that this time...

25
00:03:47,517 --> 00:03:49,137
I would protect you no matter what.

26
00:03:50,564 --> 00:03:51,564
Die!

27
00:04:00,637 --> 00:04:02,177
I still remember it.

28
00:04:22,017 --> 00:04:23,317
Kataoka-san.

29
00:04:24,765 --> 00:04:25,824
Kataoka-san!

30
00:04:28,518 --> 00:04:30,103
It hurts like hell...

31
00:04:46,328 --> 00:04:47,328
Kataoka-san.

32
00:04:48,580 --> 00:04:49,790
Kataoka-san!

33
00:04:59,317 --> 00:05:00,717
Right there in my arms,

34
00:05:03,417 --> 00:05:04,717
your warmth

35
00:05:05,917 --> 00:05:07,217
slowly faded away.

36
00:05:12,562 --> 00:05:13,980
Something like that...

37
00:05:14,917 --> 00:05:16,217
Never again...

38
00:05:24,577 --> 00:05:25,877
Asahi.

39
00:05:26,837 --> 00:05:28,137
Asahi.

40
00:05:30,700 --> 00:05:31,700
Asahi.

41
00:05:32,165 --> 00:05:33,165
Asahi.

42
00:05:34,251 --> 00:05:35,251
Asahi.

43
00:05:36,586 --> 00:05:37,587
Asahi!

44
00:05:52,018 --> 00:05:53,536
I'll protect you, Boss.

45
00:05:55,577 --> 00:05:56,877
I'll never...

46
00:05:57,777 --> 00:05:59,077
let you die.

47
00:06:17,586 --> 00:06:18,687
My old man...

48
00:06:20,317 --> 00:06:21,254
Not the former boss,

49
00:06:21,337 --> 00:06:22,637
my actual father.

50
00:06:25,077 --> 00:06:27,577
He died protecting the boss in a gang war.

51
00:06:30,432 --> 00:06:31,908
He left my mom behind.

52
00:06:33,018 --> 00:06:35,145
She wouldn't eat or sleep.

53
00:06:36,577 --> 00:06:38,214
She just cried all day long.

54
00:06:38,297 --> 00:06:39,597
She couldn't stop crying,

55
00:06:41,277 --> 00:06:42,817
and it completely broke her.

56
00:06:49,659 --> 00:06:51,553
When I stepped into the yakuza world,

57
00:06:52,597 --> 00:06:54,723
I swore I'd never settle down with a woman.

58
00:07:00,277 --> 00:07:01,917
That's why I married you.

59
00:07:05,617 --> 00:07:07,017
Because with you,

60
00:07:09,317 --> 00:07:11,317
whether we live or
die, we're in it together.

61
00:07:16,686 --> 00:07:17,996
Boss...

62
00:07:19,517 --> 00:07:23,417
Though I really did mean it about
taking responsibility for your first time.

63
00:07:27,077 --> 00:07:29,137
Do you really think you
can be the only one saved?

64
00:07:29,697 --> 00:07:30,697
Huh?

65
00:07:32,869 --> 00:07:33,662
You'll never be happy.

66
00:07:33,745 --> 00:07:34,663
You don't get to be happy.

67
00:07:34,746 --> 00:07:35,746
Kill me.

68
00:07:36,748 --> 00:07:40,674
- You'll never be happy.
- Please, kill me.

69
00:07:40,757 --> 00:07:42,838
You will never find happiness.

70
00:07:42,921 --> 00:07:44,174
Never be happy.

71
00:07:44,257 --> 00:07:45,382
Never.

72
00:07:46,277 --> 00:07:48,057
Never be happy.

73
00:07:53,097 --> 00:07:54,397
You will never

74
00:07:55,137 --> 00:07:57,334
find happiness.

75
00:07:57,417 --> 00:07:59,774
You'll never be happy.

76
00:07:59,857 --> 00:08:01,177
You don't deserve to be happy.

77
00:08:09,157 --> 00:08:10,157
Ren.

78
00:08:25,677 --> 00:08:26,856
Live on with me.

79
00:08:29,887 --> 00:08:30,969
Ren.

80
00:08:37,617 --> 00:08:38,917
Yes.

81
00:09:47,295 --> 00:09:48,313
This is taking up space.

82
00:09:49,457 --> 00:09:50,523
Take it back.

83
00:09:53,497 --> 00:09:54,797
This money is...

84
00:09:57,797 --> 00:09:59,224
There's 200 million here.

85
00:09:59,307 --> 00:10:00,600
I'm leaving the family.

86
00:10:02,237 --> 00:10:03,637
It's all yours.

87
00:10:07,557 --> 00:10:10,757
With the tribute owed to headquarters,
the Kirii-gumi must be strapped for cash.

88
00:10:11,217 --> 00:10:12,617
You didn't touch this money?

89
00:10:13,370 --> 00:10:14,670
Well...

90
00:10:17,897 --> 00:10:19,197
Who knows?

91
00:10:27,657 --> 00:10:28,554
Come on, stay a little longer.

92
00:10:28,637 --> 00:10:30,338
No way, I'm heading back to Okinawa.

93
00:10:30,421 --> 00:10:31,673
Are you really leaving?

94
00:10:31,756 --> 00:10:32,614
Yeah, for real this time.

95
00:10:32,697 --> 00:10:33,394
I'm gonna miss you.

96
00:10:33,477 --> 00:10:35,594
What's with you? Is that
all you know how to say?

97
00:10:35,677 --> 00:10:36,394
Boss.

98
00:10:36,477 --> 00:10:36,994
Huh?

99
00:10:37,077 --> 00:10:38,014
We're gonna miss you so much.

100
00:10:38,097 --> 00:10:39,397
Yeah, right.

101
00:10:40,677 --> 00:10:42,134
Alright boys, time to go.

102
00:10:42,217 --> 00:10:44,717
Don't go, Boss!

103
00:10:45,537 --> 00:10:46,954
Sorry to keep you waiting.

104
00:10:47,037 --> 00:10:49,014
Oh, all wrapped up?

105
00:10:49,097 --> 00:10:50,397
Yes.

106
00:10:51,377 --> 00:10:52,677
Ren-Ren!

107
00:10:53,897 --> 00:10:55,113
I'll stan you for the rest of my life!

108
00:10:55,137 --> 00:10:57,037
I'll drop champagne tips on your stream!

109
00:11:01,161 --> 00:11:02,328
Kataoka-san.

110
00:11:04,622 --> 00:11:05,748
Thank you for everything.

111
00:11:06,497 --> 00:11:07,667
Sure.

112
00:11:07,750 --> 00:11:09,043
Take care of yourself.

113
00:11:09,917 --> 00:11:11,217
Yes, sir.

114
00:11:16,037 --> 00:11:17,337
Boss.

115
00:11:24,309 --> 00:11:25,602
Fourth.

116
00:11:27,337 --> 00:11:28,894
Hit me up if you ever come to Okinawa.

117
00:11:28,977 --> 00:11:31,017
I'll hook you up with
double boba in your milk tea.

118
00:11:31,524 --> 00:11:33,068
Give me a break.

119
00:11:33,151 --> 00:11:34,627
I hate the heat.

120
00:11:52,879 --> 00:11:55,315
Still as impossible to read as ever.

121
00:11:57,177 --> 00:11:58,477
The Fourth...

122
00:11:59,137 --> 00:12:01,454
is actually pretty easy to read.

123
00:12:01,537 --> 00:12:02,837
Him?

124
00:12:04,017 --> 00:12:06,517
You must be pretty weird
yourself to say something like that.

125
00:12:12,857 --> 00:12:14,157
Kataoka-san.

126
00:12:17,177 --> 00:12:18,637
There's somewhere I want to go.

127
00:12:30,297 --> 00:12:31,543
Whoa! A fish just jumped!

128
00:12:31,626 --> 00:12:32,474
It's a fish!

129
00:12:32,557 --> 00:12:34,545
Odajima, did you see that? A fish!

130
00:12:41,357 --> 00:12:42,657
I missed it.

131
00:12:51,137 --> 00:12:52,737
It'd been a while since I played yakuza.

132
00:12:53,857 --> 00:12:55,157
That was actually pretty fun.

133
00:13:01,155 --> 00:13:02,448
Back to civilian life now,

134
00:13:05,523 --> 00:13:06,619
right?

135
00:13:07,829 --> 00:13:08,829
Ren.

136
00:13:13,117 --> 00:13:14,417
Yes.

137
00:13:15,897 --> 00:13:17,414
Kataoka-san.

138
00:13:17,497 --> 00:13:19,074
That was your cue to call me Kin-chan.

139
00:13:19,157 --> 00:13:20,457
Read the room, man.

140
00:13:24,617 --> 00:13:25,917
Whenever that guy...

141
00:13:27,377 --> 00:13:29,237
talked about you,

142
00:13:30,537 --> 00:13:33,771
he always called you Kataoka-san.

143
00:13:37,857 --> 00:13:39,514
Odajima.

144
00:13:39,597 --> 00:13:40,897
It's Kataoka-san.

145
00:13:42,177 --> 00:13:43,648
He's seriously so cool.

146
00:13:44,557 --> 00:13:45,557
You know,

147
00:13:46,277 --> 00:13:49,557
someday I'm gonna make it big and
rake in the cash, just like Kataoka-san.

148
00:13:52,157 --> 00:13:53,677
And then I'll build...

149
00:13:54,377 --> 00:13:56,397
a huge, fancy house for my mom.

150
00:13:57,183 --> 00:13:58,623
Man...

151
00:13:59,363 --> 00:14:01,983
I can't wait to show it to Kataoka-san.

152
00:14:19,270 --> 00:14:22,796
[TN: Asahi Kaiho's grave with
his religious "given" name on it]

153
00:14:33,623 --> 00:14:35,016
Sorry to keep you waiting.

154
00:14:38,617 --> 00:14:40,077
Let's go build that big house,

155
00:14:41,422 --> 00:14:42,465
Asahi.

156
00:14:45,635 --> 00:14:47,904
He really meant a lot to you, didn't he?

157
00:14:50,857 --> 00:14:51,949
Yes.

158
00:14:53,518 --> 00:14:54,852
More than anyone.

159
00:15:01,597 --> 00:15:02,897
I see.

160
00:15:17,177 --> 00:15:18,477
So there really are...

161
00:15:21,838 --> 00:15:23,773
three of us in this family.

162
00:15:54,620 --> 00:15:56,206
Kataoka-san.

163
00:15:56,289 --> 00:15:57,289
Hmm?

164
00:15:58,397 --> 00:15:59,874
Someday,

165
00:15:59,957 --> 00:16:01,257
would it be okay if I told you?

166
00:16:02,477 --> 00:16:03,777
Everything about me.

167
00:16:05,297 --> 00:16:06,299
Sure.

168
00:16:06,917 --> 00:16:08,377
Whenever you're ready to talk,

169
00:16:09,577 --> 00:16:11,337
we've got all the time in the world.

170
00:16:12,457 --> 00:16:14,277
Until we're both old and gray,

171
00:16:16,017 --> 00:16:17,017
right?

172
00:16:20,337 --> 00:16:21,737
Come to think of it,

173
00:16:22,937 --> 00:16:24,337
on our very first trip together,

174
00:16:26,037 --> 00:16:29,271
you were actually trying
to kill me, weren't you?

175
00:16:33,137 --> 00:16:35,337
I don't know how many decades it'll take,

176
00:16:36,897 --> 00:16:38,617
but if you stick with me till the very end,

177
00:16:42,877 --> 00:16:44,757
you'll get to watch me
die with your own eyes.

178
00:17:00,497 --> 00:17:02,277
That's going to be a long wait.

179
00:17:03,857 --> 00:17:06,057
Which means we get to be
together that much longer.

180
00:17:13,157 --> 00:17:15,937
Oh, right. You still
haven't kissed me first.

181
00:17:18,016 --> 00:17:19,316
You still remember that?

182
00:17:20,097 --> 00:17:21,397
Of course I do.

183
00:18:07,253 --> 00:18:08,421
Kataoka-san.

184
00:18:09,417 --> 00:18:10,590
That's too long.

185
00:18:12,517 --> 00:18:14,174
What if someone sees us...

186
00:18:14,257 --> 00:18:15,934
Who cares?

187
00:18:16,017 --> 00:18:17,317
We're married.

188
00:18:24,417 --> 00:18:25,772
Kataoka-san.

189
00:18:25,855 --> 00:18:26,855
Hmm?

190
00:18:40,177 --> 00:18:41,987
Where did this money come from?

191
00:18:42,913 --> 00:18:43,913
Uh...

192
00:18:45,077 --> 00:18:46,794
Did you sneak this out of the bag?

193
00:18:46,877 --> 00:18:48,957
I blew all my horse racing winnings.

194
00:18:50,703 --> 00:18:51,703
What?

195
00:18:53,317 --> 00:18:54,214
Oh?

196
00:18:54,297 --> 00:18:55,074
Hand it over!

197
00:18:55,157 --> 00:18:56,457
No way!

198
00:18:57,157 --> 00:18:58,457
Not happening!

199
00:22:05,577 --> 00:22:06,877
Man...

200
00:22:07,657 --> 00:22:09,537
I can't believe it went under.

201
00:22:10,517 --> 00:22:12,037
The old man's shop.

202
00:22:12,677 --> 00:22:13,677
Yeah.

203
00:22:14,542 --> 00:22:16,268
That really caught me off guard.

204
00:22:17,257 --> 00:22:18,257
Yes.

205
00:22:19,217 --> 00:22:21,815
Looks like the old man is
stepping down as boss, too.

206
00:22:23,057 --> 00:22:24,057
Yes.

207
00:22:25,997 --> 00:22:27,297
Hey, wait a second.

208
00:22:28,597 --> 00:22:30,897
Have you been saying nothing
but "yes" this whole time?

209
00:22:32,557 --> 00:22:33,557
Yes.

210
00:22:34,937 --> 00:22:38,094
Seriously, what are we supposed to do now?

211
00:22:38,177 --> 00:22:40,401
Even our place belongs to the old man.

212
00:22:40,484 --> 00:22:42,570
Just like that, we're both
jobless and homeless.

213
00:22:45,737 --> 00:22:47,197
Should we go back to being yakuza?

214
00:22:48,857 --> 00:22:49,857
Huh?

215
00:22:50,397 --> 00:22:51,697
Just kidding.

216
00:22:53,577 --> 00:22:55,794
Your jokes never sound like jokes at all.

217
00:22:55,877 --> 00:22:57,177
Honestly, they're terrible.

218
00:22:58,117 --> 00:22:59,417
My bad.

219
00:23:04,117 --> 00:23:05,717
No matter what happens, we'll be fine.

220
00:23:06,337 --> 00:23:07,344
Huh?

221
00:23:09,057 --> 00:23:10,394
Because we...

222
00:23:10,477 --> 00:23:11,777
are free.

223
00:23:14,137 --> 00:23:15,437
You're right about that.

224
00:23:28,677 --> 00:23:29,754
Where to now?

225
00:23:29,837 --> 00:23:31,174
I'm starving.

226
00:23:31,257 --> 00:23:32,754
Let's go grab some sushi.

227
00:23:32,837 --> 00:23:34,137
We're broke, remember?

228
00:23:40,557 --> 00:23:41,587
If...

229
00:23:42,377 --> 00:23:43,937
there's really such a thing as forever,

230
00:23:45,057 --> 00:23:46,775
then it's this journey to killing you.

231
00:24:21,117 --> 00:24:23,157
(The End)
